\id LAM American King James Version

\usfm 3.1
\h Lamentations
\toc1 The Lamentations of Jeremiah
\toc2 Lamentations
\toc3 Lam
\mt1 THE LAMENTATIONS OF JEREMIAH
\c 1
\p \v 1 How does the city sit solitary, \add that was\add* full of people! \add how\add* is she become as a widow! she \add that was\add* great among the nations, \add and\add* princess among the provinces, \add how\add* is she become tributary!
\m \v 2 She weeps sore in the night, and her tears \add are\add* on her cheeks: among all her lovers she has none to comfort \add her\add*: all her friends have dealt treacherously with her, they are become her enemies.
\m \v 3 Judah is gone into captivity because of affliction, and because of great servitude: she dwells among the heathen, she finds no rest: all her persecutors overtook her between the straits.
\m \v 4 The ways of Zion do mourn, because none come to the solemn feasts: all her gates are desolate: her priests sigh, her virgins are afflicted, and she \add is\add* in bitterness.
\m \v 5 Her adversaries are the chief, her enemies prosper; for the LORD has afflicted her for the multitude of her transgressions: her children are gone into captivity before the enemy.
\m \v 6 And from the daughter of Zion all her beauty is departed: her princes are become like harts \add that\add* find no pasture, and they are gone without strength before the pursuer.
\m \v 7 Jerusalem remembered in the days of her affliction and of her miseries all her pleasant things that she had in the days of old, when her people fell into the hand of the enemy, and none did help her: the adversaries saw her, \add and\add* did mock at her sabbaths.
\m \v 8 Jerusalem has grievously sinned; therefore she is removed: all that honored her despise her, because they have seen her nakedness: yes, she sighs, and turns backward.
\m \v 9 Her filthiness \add is\add* in her skirts; she remembers not her last end; therefore she came down wonderfully: she had no comforter. O LORD, behold my affliction: for the enemy has magnified \add himself\add*.
\m \v 10 The adversary has spread out his hand on all her pleasant things: for she has seen \add that\add* the heathen entered into her sanctuary, whom you did command \add that\add* they should not enter into your congregation.
\m \v 11 All her people sigh, they seek bread; they have given their pleasant things for meat to relieve the soul: see, O LORD, and consider; for I am become vile.
\m \v 12 \add Is it\add* nothing to you, all you that pass by? behold, and see if there be any sorrow like to my sorrow, which is done to me, with which the LORD has afflicted \add me\add* in the day of his fierce anger.
\m \v 13 From above has he sent fire into my bones, and it prevails against them: he has spread a net for my feet, he has turned me back: he has made me desolate \add and\add* faint all the day.
\m \v 14 The yoke of my transgressions is bound by his hand: they are wreathed, \add and\add* come up on my neck: he has made my strength to fall, the LORD has delivered me into \add their\add* hands, \add from whom\add* I am not able to rise up.
\m \v 15 The LORD has trodden under foot all my mighty \add men\add* in the middle of me: he has called an assembly against me to crush my young men: the LORD has trodden the virgin, the daughter of Judah, \add as\add* in a wine press.
\m \v 16 For these \add things\add* I weep; my eye, my eye runs down with water, because the comforter that should relieve my soul is far from me: my children are desolate, because the enemy prevailed.
\m \v 17 Zion spreads forth her hands, \add and there is\add* none to comfort her: the LORD has commanded concerning Jacob, \add that\add* his adversaries \add should be\add* round about him: Jerusalem is as a menstruous woman among them.
\m \v 18 The LORD is righteous; for I have rebelled against his commandment: hear, I pray you, all people, and behold my sorrow: my virgins and my young men are gone into captivity.
\m \v 19 I called for my lovers, \add but\add* they deceived me: my priests and my elders gave up the ghost in the city, while they sought their meat to relieve their souls.
\m \v 20 Behold, O LORD; for I \add am\add* in distress: my bowels are troubled; my heart is turned within me; for I have grievously rebelled: abroad the sword bereaves, at home \add there is\add* as death.
\m \v 21 They have heard that I sigh: \add there is\add* none to comfort me: all my enemies have heard of my trouble; they are glad that you have done \add it\add*: you will bring the day \add that\add* you have called, and they shall be like to me.
\m \v 22 Let all their wickedness come before you; and do to them, as you have done to me for all my transgressions: for my sighs \add are\add* many, and my heart \add is\add* faint.
\c 2
\p \v 1 How has the LORD covered the daughter of Zion with a cloud in his anger, \add and\add* cast down from heaven to the earth the beauty of Israel, and remembered not his footstool in the day of his anger!
\m \v 2 The LORD has swallowed up all the habitations of Jacob, and has not pitied: he has thrown down in his wrath the strong holds of the daughter of Judah; he has brought \add them\add* down to the ground: he has polluted the kingdom and the princes thereof.
\m \v 3 He has cut off in \add his\add* fierce anger all the horn of Israel: he has drawn back his right hand from before the enemy, and he burned against Jacob like a flaming fire, \add which\add* devours round about.
\m \v 4 He has bent his bow like an enemy: he stood with his right hand as an adversary, and slew all \add that were\add* pleasant to the eye in the tabernacle of the daughter of Zion: he poured out his fury like fire.
\m \v 5 The LORD was as an enemy: he has swallowed up Israel, he has swallowed up all her palaces: he has destroyed his strong holds, and has increased in the daughter of Judah mourning and lamentation.
\m \v 6 And he has violently taken away his tabernacle, as \add if it were of\add* a garden: he has destroyed his places of the assembly: the LORD has caused the solemn feasts and sabbaths to be forgotten in Zion, and has despised in the indignation of his anger the king and the priest.
\m \v 7 The LORD has cast off his altar, he has abhorred his sanctuary, he has given up into the hand of the enemy the walls of her palaces; they have made a noise in the house of the LORD, as in the day of a solemn feast.
\m \v 8 The LORD has purposed to destroy the wall of the daughter of Zion: he has stretched out a line, he has not withdrawn his hand from destroying: therefore he made the rampart and the wall to lament; they languished together.
\m \v 9 Her gates are sunk into the ground; he has destroyed and broken her bars: her king and her princes \add are\add* among the Gentiles: the law \add is\add* no \add more\add*; her prophets also find no vision from the LORD.
\m \v 10 The elders of the daughter of Zion sit on the ground, \add and\add* keep silence: they have cast up dust on their heads; they have girded themselves with sackcloth: the virgins of Jerusalem hang down their heads to the ground.
\m \v 11 My eyes do fail with tears, my bowels are troubled, my liver is poured on the earth, for the destruction of the daughter of my people; because the children and the sucklings swoon in the streets of the city.
\m \v 12 They say to their mothers, Where \add is\add* corn and wine? when they swooned as the wounded in the streets of the city, when their soul was poured out into their mothers' bosom.
\m \v 13 What thing shall I take to witness for you? what thing shall I liken to you, O daughter of Jerusalem? what shall I equal to you, that I may comfort you, O virgin daughter of Zion? for your breach \add is\add* great like the sea: who can heal you?
\m \v 14 Your prophets have seen vain and foolish things for you: and they have not discovered your iniquity, to turn away your captivity; but have seen for you false burdens and causes of banishment.
\m \v 15 All that pass by clap \add their\add* hands at you; they hiss and wag their head at the daughter of Jerusalem, \add saying\add*, \add Is\add* this the city that \add men\add* call The perfection of beauty, The joy of the whole earth?
\m \v 16 All your enemies have opened their mouth against you: they hiss and gnash the teeth: they say, We have swallowed \add her\add* up: certainly this \add is\add* the day that we looked for; we have found, we have seen \add it\add*.
\m \v 17 The LORD has done \add that\add* which he had devised; he has fulfilled his word that he had commanded in the days of old: he has thrown down, and has not pitied: and he has caused \add your\add* enemy to rejoice over you, he has set up the horn of your adversaries.
\m \v 18 Their heart cried to the LORD, O wall of the daughter of Zion, let tears run down like a river day and night: give yourself no rest; let not the apple of your eye cease.
\m \v 19 Arise, cry out in the night: in the beginning of the watches pour out your heart like water before the face of the LORD: lift up your hands toward him for the life of your young children, that faint for hunger in the top of every street.
\m \v 20 Behold, O LORD, and consider to whom you have done this. Shall the women eat their fruit, \add and\add* children of a span long? shall the priest and the prophet be slain in the sanctuary of the Lord?
\m \v 21 The young and the old lie on the ground in the streets: my virgins and my young men are fallen by the sword; you have slain \add them\add* in the day of your anger; you have killed, \add and\add* not pitied.
\m \v 22 You have called as in a solemn day my terrors round about, so that in the day of the LORD's anger none escaped nor remained: those that I have swaddled and brought up has my enemy consumed.
\c 3
\p \v 1 I \add AM\add* the man \add that\add* has seen affliction by the rod of his wrath.
\m \v 2 He has led me, and brought \add me into\add* darkness, but not \add into\add* light.
\m \v 3 Surely against me is he turned; he turns his hand \add against me\add* all the day.
\m \v 4 My flesh and my skin has he made old; he has broken my bones.
\m \v 5 He has built against me, and compassed \add me\add* with gall and travail.
\m \v 6 He has set me in dark places, as \add they that be\add* dead of old.
\m \v 7 He has hedged me about, that I cannot get out: he has made my chain heavy.
\m \v 8 Also when I cry and shout, he shuts out my prayer.
\m \v 9 He has enclosed my ways with hewn stone, he has made my paths crooked.
\m \v 10 He \add was\add* to me \add as\add* a bear lying in wait, \add and as\add* a lion in secret places.
\m \v 11 He has turned aside my ways, and pulled me in pieces: he has made me desolate.
\m \v 12 He has bent his bow, and set me as a mark for the arrow.
\m \v 13 He has caused the arrows of his quiver to enter into my reins.
\m \v 14 I was a derision to all my people; \add and\add* their song all the day.
\m \v 15 He has filled me with bitterness, he has made me drunken with wormwood.
\m \v 16 He has also broken my teeth with gravel stones, he has covered me with ashes.
\m \v 17 And you have removed my soul far off from peace: I forgot prosperity.
\m \v 18 And I said, My strength and my hope is perished from the LORD:
\m \v 19 Remembering my affliction and my misery, the wormwood and the gall.
\m \v 20 My soul has \add them\add* still in remembrance, and is humbled in me.
\m \v 21 This I recall to my mind, therefore have I hope.
\m \v 22 \add It is of\add* the LORD's mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not.
\m \v 23 \add They are\add* new every morning: great \add is\add* your faithfulness.
\m \v 24 The LORD \add is\add* my portion, said my soul; therefore will I hope in him.
\m \v 25 The LORD \add is\add* good to them that wait for him, to the soul \add that\add* seeks him.
\m \v 26 \add It is\add* good that \add a man\add* should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD.
\m \v 27 \add It is\add* good for a man that he bear the yoke of his youth.
\m \v 28 He sits alone and keeps silence, because he has borne \add it\add* on him.
\m \v 29 He puts his mouth in the dust; if so be there may be hope.
\m \v 30 He gives \add his\add* cheek to him that smites him: he is filled full with reproach.
\m \v 31 For the LORD will not cast off for ever:
\m \v 32 But though he cause grief, yet will he have compassion according to the multitude of his mercies.
\m \v 33 For he does not afflict willingly nor grieve the children of men.
\m \v 34 To crush under his feet all the prisoners of the earth.
\m \v 35 To turn aside the right of a man before the face of the most High,
\m \v 36 To subvert a man in his cause, the LORD approves not.
\m \v 37 Who \add is\add* he \add that\add* said, and it comes to pass, \add when\add* the Lord commands \add it\add* not?
\m \v 38 Out of the mouth of the most High proceeds not evil and good?
\m \v 39 Why does a living man complain, a man for the punishment of his sins?
\m \v 40 Let us search and try our ways, and turn again to the LORD.
\m \v 41 Let us lift up our heart with \add our\add* hands to God in the heavens.
\m \v 42 We have transgressed and have rebelled: you have not pardoned.
\m \v 43 You have covered with anger, and persecuted us: you have slain, you have not pitied.
\m \v 44 You have covered yourself with a cloud, that \add our\add* prayer should not pass through.
\m \v 45 You have made us \add as\add* the offscouring and refuse in the middle of the people.
\m \v 46 All our enemies have opened their mouths against us.
\m \v 47 Fear and a snare is come on us, desolation and destruction.
\m \v 48 My eye runs down with rivers of water for the destruction of the daughter of my people.
\m \v 49 My eye trickles down, and ceases not, without any intermission.
\m \v 50 Till the LORD look down, and behold from heaven.
\m \v 51 My eye affects my heart because of all the daughters of my city.
\m \v 52 My enemies chased me sore, like a bird, without cause.
\m \v 53 They have cut off my life in the dungeon, and cast a stone on me.
\m \v 54 Waters flowed over my head; \add then\add* I said, I am cut off.
\m \v 55 I called on your name, O LORD, out of the low dungeon.
\m \v 56 You have heard my voice: hide not your ear at my breathing, at my cry.
\m \v 57 You drew near in the day \add that\add* I called on you: you said, Fear not.
\m \v 58 O LORD, you have pleaded the causes of my soul; you have redeemed my life.
\m \v 59 O LORD, you have seen my wrong: judge you my cause.
\m \v 60 You have seen all their vengeance \add and\add* all their imaginations against me.
\m \v 61 You have heard their reproach, O LORD, \add and\add* all their imaginations against me;
\m \v 62 The lips of those that rose up against me, and their device against me all the day.
\m \v 63 Behold their sitting down, and their rising up; I \add am\add* their music.
\m \v 64 Render to them a recompense, O LORD, according to the work of their hands.
\m \v 65 Give them sorrow of heart, your curse to them.
\m \v 66 Persecute and destroy them in anger from under the heavens of the LORD.
\c 4
\p \v 1 How is the gold become dim! \add how\add* is the most fine gold changed! the stones of the sanctuary are poured out in the top of every street.
\m \v 2 The precious sons of Zion, comparable to fine gold, how are they esteemed as earthen pitchers, the work of the hands of the potter!
\m \v 3 Even the sea monsters draw out the breast, they give suck to their young ones: the daughter of my people \add is become\add* cruel, like the ostriches in the wilderness.
\m \v 4 The tongue of the sucking child sticks to the roof of his mouth for thirst: the young children ask bread, \add and\add* no man breaks \add it\add* to them.
\m \v 5 They that did feed delicately are desolate in the streets: they that were brought up in scarlet embrace dunghills.
\m \v 6 For the punishment of the iniquity of the daughter of my people is greater than the punishment of the sin of Sodom, that was overthrown as in a moment, and no hands stayed on her.
\m \v 7 Her Nazarites were purer than snow, they were whiter than milk, they were more ruddy in body than rubies, their polishing \add was\add* of sapphire:
\m \v 8 Their visage is blacker than a coal; they are not known in the streets: their skin sticks to their bones; it is withered, it is become like a stick.
\m \v 9 \add They that be\add* slain with the sword are better than \add they that be\add* slain with hunger: for these pine away, stricken through for \add want of\add* the fruits of the field.
\m \v 10 The hands of the pitiful women have sodden their own children: they were their meat in the destruction of the daughter of my people.
\m \v 11 The LORD has accomplished his fury; he has poured out his fierce anger, and has kindled a fire in Zion, and it has devoured the foundations thereof.
\m \v 12 The kings of the earth, and all the inhabitants of the world, would not have believed that the adversary and the enemy should have entered into the gates of Jerusalem.
\m \v 13 For the sins of her prophets, \add and\add* the iniquities of her priests, that have shed the blood of the just in the middle of her,
\m \v 14 They have wandered \add as\add* blind \add men\add* in the streets, they have polluted themselves with blood, so that men could not touch their garments.
\m \v 15 They cried to them, Depart you; \add it is\add* unclean; depart, depart, touch not: when they fled away and wandered, they said among the heathen, They shall no more sojourn \add there\add*.
\m \v 16 The anger of the LORD has divided them; he will no more regard them: they respected not the persons of the priests, they favored not the elders.
\m \v 17 As for us, our eyes as yet failed for our vain help: in our watching we have watched for a nation \add that\add* could not save \add us\add*.
\m \v 18 They hunt our steps, that we cannot go in our streets: our end is near, our days are fulfilled; for our end is come.
\m \v 19 Our persecutors are swifter than the eagles of the heaven: they pursued us on the mountains, they laid wait for us in the wilderness.
\m \v 20 The breath of our nostrils, the anointed of the LORD, was taken in their pits, of whom we said, Under his shadow we shall live among the heathen.
\m \v 21 Rejoice and be glad, O daughter of Edom, that dwell in the land of Uz; the cup also shall pass through to you: you shall be drunken, and shall make yourself naked.
\m \v 22 The punishment of your iniquity is accomplished, O daughter of Zion; he will no more carry you away into captivity: he will visit your iniquity, O daughter of Edom; he will discover your sins.
\c 5
\p \v 1 Remember, O LORD, what is come on us: consider, and behold our reproach.
\m \v 2 Our inheritance is turned to strangers, our houses to aliens.
\m \v 3 We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers \add are\add* as widows.
\m \v 4 We have drunken our water for money; our wood is sold to us.
\m \v 5 Our necks \add are\add* under persecution: we labor, \add and\add* have no rest.
\m \v 6 We have given the hand \add to\add* the Egyptians, \add and to\add* the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread.
\m \v 7 Our fathers have sinned, \add and are\add* not; and we have borne their iniquities.
\m \v 8 Servants have ruled over us: \add there is\add* none that does deliver \add us\add* out of their hand.
\m \v 9 We got our bread with \add the peril of\add* our lives because of the sword of the wilderness.
\m \v 10 Our skin was black like an oven because of the terrible famine.
\m \v 11 They ravished the women in Zion, \add and\add* the maids in the cities of Judah.
\m \v 12 Princes are hanged up by their hand: the faces of elders were not honored.
\m \v 13 They took the young men to grind, and the children fell under the wood.
\m \v 14 The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their music.
\m \v 15 The joy of our heart is ceased; our dance is turned into mourning.
\m \v 16 The crown is fallen \add from\add* our head: woe to us, that we have sinned!
\m \v 17 For this our heart is faint; for these \add things\add* our eyes are dim.
\m \v 18 Because of the mountain of Zion, which is desolate, the foxes walk on it.
\m \v 19 You, O LORD, remain for ever; your throne from generation to generation.
\m \v 20 Why do you forget us for ever, \add and\add* forsake us so long time?
\m \v 21 Turn you us to you, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old.
\m \v 22 But you have utterly rejected us; you are very wroth against us.
